Third-party components
================================================================================

This product includes a vendored, unmodified copy of the "core" writer
library from SourcetrailDB:

    SourcetrailDB
    https://github.com/CoatiSoftware/SourcetrailDB
    Copyright 2018 Coati Software SYMHOW
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The vendored source lives under third_party/sourcetraildb/ (include/, src/,
cpp_sqlite/). See third_party/sourcetraildb/LICENSE.txt for the full license
text, third_party/sourcetraildb/AUTHORS.txt for upstream authorship, and
third_party/sourcetraildb/PROVENANCE.md for exactly what was copied, what
was hand-written, and (if any) what was patched.

This product also depends on, but does not vendor or redistribute source
for, the following third-party libraries, obtained at build time via the
project's flox environment:

    - LLVM/libclang (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception / NCSA)
    - SQLite (public domain)
    - nlohmann/json (MIT)
    - Catch2 (BSL-1.0), test-only dependency

================================================================================
Implementation provenance
================================================================================

symhow's own indexing and query-engine logic (everything outside of
third_party/) is an original, independently authored implementation. It was designed
and written based on publicly available documentation (the libclang C API,
the SQLite documentation, the Sourcetrail/SourcetrailDB project's published
database schema and file format as embodied in the Apache-2.0-licensed
SourcetrailDB writer library vendored above) and independent analysis of
the externally observable behavior of Sourcetrail (the Sourcetrail
application itself is GPLv3-licensed). Upstream changes may be inspected
during compatibility and performance reviews, but no source code from
Sourcetrail (the GPLv3 application) is copied or incorporated into symhow.
